# The Dockerfile COPYs the repo then runs `pnpm install` fresh inside the
# container, so local install/build artifacts are never needed as build
# context and only bloat/slow the upload — pnpm's node_modules is full of
# symlinks that can break Docker's context tar entirely, which is what this
# file exists to prevent.
#
# NOTE: unlike .gitignore, Docker's ignore patterns are NOT recursive by
# default — a bare `node_modules/` only matches at the context root. Every
# pattern below is prefixed with **/ so it matches at any depth too.

**/.tools/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.next/
**/out/
**/next-env.d.ts
**/coverage/
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/.local/
**/*.log
**/npm-debug.log*
**/pnpm-debug.log*
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/.vscode/*
!**/.vscode/extensions.json
**/gitleaks-report.json
.git/
.claude/
